  "description": "USDA Forest Service Wildfire Risk to Communities landscape-wide risk components (RDS-2020-0016-2, published 2024) as downloaded by `_shared/scripts/download_raw.sh wildfire-risk-to-communities` from the Forest Service Research Data Archive. Eight 30 m GeoTIFF layers: BP (burn probability); CFL (conditional flame length); CRPS (conditional risk to potential structures); Exposure (exposure type); FLEP4 (flame length exceedance probability, 4 ft); FLEP8 (flame length exceedance probability, 8 ft); RPS (risk to potential structures); WHP (wildfire hazard potential). One zip per layer for CONUS, plus one zip each for Alaska and Hawaii holding all eight layers. The Archive's other per-state zips repeat the CONUS rasters and are not mirrored; their URLs are on the DOI landing page. Built from LANDFIRE 2020 (version 2.2.0) fuels and FSim burn probability; the FGDC metadata gives a ground-condition date of 2020-12-31. Read-only.",
